can [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]specify round-robin pools and ordered fallback chains through a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]guided, keyboard-driven builder instead of hand-typed free text, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the temporary-override path refuses selector expressions instead of[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]silently persisting a corrupted single target, and the docs [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]describe the shipped behavior.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]models_panel_pool_authoring.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/models_panel_pool_authoring.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-lz[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-lz/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reject selector expressions in the temporary-override path[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]override-selector-reject[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]override-selector-reject: detect selector syntax with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]parse_model_alias_selector in the panel's Custom Override Model flow and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]refuse it with a message pointing at the persistent Edit key, instead of[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]letting a pool string split on its first slash and persist a bogus [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]single-target override.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Parse-based selector detection and prefilled custom input[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]selector-edit-plumbing[dim] · [dim][/dim]after override-selector-reject[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]selector-edit-plumbing: add a shared TUI selector helper module over the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]existing llm_provider API, replace the substring selector sniffing in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the alias Edit flow with real parsing plus per-member safety checks, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]give the custom-model input an initial value so editing an existing [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]selector no longer means retyping it.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Guided pool and fallback builder modal[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]selector-builder[dim] · [dim][/dim]after selector-edit-plumbing[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]selector-builder: add a SelectorBuilderModal that assembles selector [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]members from the existing model picker and effort ladder with add, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]remove, reorder, per-member effort, and pool-versus-fallback toggling, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate member selection against nested selectors, and route a new picker [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]entry row through it into the unchanged preview and write path.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation sync for selector authoring[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]selector-docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after selector-builder[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]selector-docs: correct the ACE Models panel documentation that claims [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the custom input only accepts concrete model strings, document the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]builder row and its keys, state that temporary overrides refuse [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]selectors, and cross-check the selector semantics and configuration [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]references.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epi